    <p class="section-no mb-6">[11] ORIGIN · FIG 01 — BIELAWA, LOWER SILESIA</p>
    <figure class="mb-10 reveal"><div class="duotone hairline overflow-hidden"><img src="/images/photos/origin-truck-1400.webp" width="1400" height="933" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Pete sitting against the race truck wheel in work gloves and sunglasses, race week 2019" class="block w-full h-auto" /></div><figcaption class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.15em] uppercase text-ink-faint mt-3">2019 · Atherton Bikes · race week, between runs</figcaption></figure>
    <div class="font-serif text-ink text-xl md:text-2xl leading-relaxed space-y-6 reveal">
      <p>I raced before I wrenched. Junior road for Poland, then the UK, then downhill. I know what a bad setup feels like from the saddle.</p>
      <p>Home is Bielawa, a textile town under the Owl Mountains. My grandfather Józef built radios at the Diora factory in the next town, and I grew up on a smuggled ZX Spectrum. That habit never left: the apps my team runs on for race settings, jig setups and race-plan timing, I wrote myself. No formal training. A mechanic who wanted better tools than a spreadsheet.</p>
      <p>First World Cup: Maribor 2007, with Mojo Suspension. Twenty seasons later I’m still in the pits, and everyone there calls me Polish Pete.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="font-mono text-[10px] text-ink-faint mt-8 tracking-[0.15em]">FIG 01 · ZX SPECTRUM → COMMODORE → AMIGA → THE PIT WALL</p>
